--- a/docs/victoriametrics/relabeling.md
+++ b/docs/victoriametrics/relabeling.md
@@ -304,6 +304,21 @@ Beside enhancements, VictoriaMetrics also provides the following new actions:
   ([Try it](https://play.victoriametrics.com/select/0/prometheus/graph/#/relabeling?config=-+action%3A+graphite%0A++match%3A+%27*.server.*.total%27%0A++labels%3A%0A++++__name__%3A+%27%24%7B2%7D_total%27%0A++++instance%3A+%27%24%7B2%7D%3A9100%27%0A++++job%3A+%27%241%27&labels=%7B__name__%3D%22app1.server.requests.total%22%7D)).
   See [Graphite Relabeling](#graphite-relabeling) for details.
 
+- **`uppercase` / `lowercase` actions**: Store the uppercased / lowercased
+  value of `source_labels` (joined with `separator`) at `target_label`.
+
+- **`trim` action**: Strips leading and trailing whitespace from the value of
+  `source_labels` (joined with `separator`) and stores the result at
+  `target_label`. This is useful when a label value ends up with stray
+  whitespace, e.g. because it was copied from a source that adds a trailing
+  newline, or because several source label values were concatenated together:
+
+  ```yaml {hl_lines=[1]}
+  - action: trim
+    source_labels: ["instance"]
+    target_label: instance
+  ```
+
 ### Graphite Relabeling
 
 VictoriaMetrics components support `action: graphite` relabeling rules. These
